WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.727
A point and a plane
Find the distance from M, with coordinates one, one, one, to the plane whose
equation is x plus two y plus two z minus six equal to zero.

2
00:00:15.727 --> 00:00:28.727
Read the normal vector
First read the normal vector from the coefficients of x, y, and z. It is one,
two, two. This vector is nonzero.

3
00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:42.636
Calculate the norm
Its norm is the square root of one squared plus two squared plus two squared.
The sum is nine, whose square root is three.

4
00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:55.636
Evaluate at point M
Substitute M's coordinates into the equation. One plus two plus two minus six
gives minus one. This is not yet the distance.

5
00:00:55.636 --> 00:01:07.727
Apply the formula
Take the absolute value of minus one and divide by the normal vector's norm.
One third is the required distance.

6
00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:23.909
A distance is nonnegative
The result is positive, which makes sense because M lies outside the plane.
The absolute value is essential. Distance cannot be negative, even when
substitution gives a negative value.
